//! | Sparse records in a global header | GNU tar applies them to the next member; bsdtar fails; Go reads a file of the stored data | refused in every mode ([`Sparse`](crate::ErrorKind::Sparse)([`Global`](crate::SparseFlaw::Global))) | `sparse/sparse-records-in-a-global-header` |
