//!
//! # Global headers
//!
//! A global header's records apply to every later member for GNU tar and
//! Python, and to none for Go. [`GlobalHeaders`](crate::GlobalHeaders)
//! chooses which family a program reads as, or refuses a global header that
//! would change a member (the default). bsdtar applied none as well until
//! libarchive 3.8.10, which refuses an archive from a global header carrying
//! any record but `comment` on, wherever it falls: there,
//! [`Defer`](crate::GlobalHeaders::Defer) reads as Go alone does.
//!
//! | Archive | Reference readers | ferrotape | Cases |
//! | --- | --- | --- | --- |
//! | A global header carrying any record but `comment` | GNU tar and Python apply its records; Go applies none; bsdtar refuses the archive from that header on, listing only the members before it | Refuse: refused ([`GlobalRecord`](crate::ErrorKind::GlobalRecord)); Apply: applied, as GNU tar and Python apply it; Defer: none applied, as Go reads it | `global/global-owner-names`, `global/a-global-link-target`, `global/a-global-path-each-member-overrides`, `global/a-global-header-in-a-v7-header`, `global/a-global-hdrcharset`, `global/a-global-path-after-a-member`, `global/a-global-path-after-the-last-member` |
//! | A global header giving a keyword twice, with different values | GNU tar applies the first and Python the last; Go applies neither, and bsdtar refuses the archive | Refuse: refused ([`GlobalRecord`](crate::ErrorKind::GlobalRecord)) unless the keyword is `comment`; Apply: refused ([`RepeatedKeyword`](crate::ErrorKind::RepeatedKeyword)); Defer: Strict refused, as for a member's own header, Compatible none applied | `global/a-global-path-given-twice`, `global/a-global-link-target-given-twice` |
//! | A global header with no records | bsdtar fails there, extracting nothing after it; GNU tar, Python and Go read on | refused in every mode ([`EmptyMetadata`](crate::ErrorKind::EmptyMetadata)) | `global/an-empty-global-header` |
//! | A global `size`, a vendor keyword, an empty value, or a second global header once one has set a member's record | GNU tar and Python read them differently (GNU tar replaces where Python merges) | Refuse and Apply: refused ([`GlobalRecord`](crate::ErrorKind::GlobalRecord), [`SecondGlobal`](crate::ErrorKind::SecondGlobal)); Defer: none applied | `global/a-global-size-and-path`, `global/a-global-extended-attribute`, `global/an-empty-global-uid-after-a-global-uid` |
//! | A global header while a pax header, a long name, a long link or another global header waits for its member | bsdtar fails on two global headers in a row; Go lets a global header consume a waiting pax header; GNU tar and Python read on, and differ | refused in every mode ([`GlobalBetweenMetadata`](crate::ErrorKind::GlobalBetweenMetadata), [`RepeatedMetadata`](crate::ErrorKind::RepeatedMetadata)) | `global/two-global-headers-before-a-member`, `global/two-global-comments-before-a-member`, `global/a-global-header-after-a-pax-header` |
